{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "כי תוליד", :translit "ki tolid", :gloss "when you give birth"} {:he "כ\"י", :translit "kaf yod", :gloss "21"} {:he "פסל מיכה", :translit "pesel mikha", :gloss "idol of Micah"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "כי תוליד", :b "פסל מיכה"}], :frame {:text "The idol of Micah is described in Judges 17–18. After Joshua's death, the tribe of Dan seized Micah's idol and set it up in Laish, and Jonathan son of Gershom served as its priest. The Talmud calculates that this idolatry persisted from the era of Joshua until the time of the Ark's capture (Bava Batra 109b). Rashi on Judges 18:30, citing the Talmud, explains the modified name מנשה as a marker of Jonathan's descent. The phrase 'after his death' in the comment refers to Moses: Moses died and the Israelites entered the land under Joshua (Deuteronomy 34:5; Joshua 1:1–2).", :sources ["Judges 17:1–6" "Judges 18:30–31" "Bava Batra 109b" "Rashi on Judges 18:30" "Deuteronomy 34:5" "Joshua 1:1–2"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "כי תוליד", :a-value 480, :b "פסל מיכה", :b-value 245, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:34:22.873479855Z", :model "glm-5.2"}